**Protocol → GUI Update Flow:**

**1. Response Received:**
```actionscript
// GameClient.as
mainBuffer.uncompress();
var response:Object = mainBuffer.readObject();
dispatchEvent(new DataEvent(response));
```

**2. Handler Processing:**
```actionscript
// CommandHandler.as
function onDataReceived(event:DataEvent):void {
    var cmd:String = event.data.cmd;  // e.g., "city.updateResource"
    var data:Object = event.data.data;

    // Route to appropriate manager
    switch(cmd) {
        case "city.updateResource":
            CityManager.updateResources(data);
            break;
        case "army.marchUpdate":
            ArmyManager.updateMarch(data);
            break;
    }
}
```

**3. Model Update:**
```actionscript
// CityManager.as
function updateResources(data:Object):void {
    currentCity.gold = data.gold;
    currentCity.food = data.food;
    // Dispatch update event
    dispatchEvent(new CityEvent(CityEvent.RESOURCES_CHANGED));
}
```

**4. GUI Listening:**
```actionscript
// ResourcePanel.as
CityManager.addEventListener(CityEvent.RESOURCES_CHANGED, onResourcesChanged);

function onResourcesChanged(e:CityEvent):void {
    goldLabel.text = CityManager.currentCity.gold.toString();
    foodLabel.text = CityManager.currentCity.food.toString();
}
```

**Pattern:** Observer/Event-driven MVC

**SharedObject.getLocal() Security Failure:**

**Causes of Failure:**
1. User disabled local storage in Flash settings
2. Storage quota exceeded
3. Sandbox restrictions (different domains)
4. Disk write permissions

**What Happens:**
```actionscript
// EvonyClient.as line 55 area
var so:SharedObject = SharedObject.getLocal("evonyData");
// If fails, so is null or throws error
```

**Error Handling:**
```actionscript
try {
    var so:SharedObject = SharedObject.getLocal("evonyData");
    if (so == null) {
        // Fallback to session-only data
        useSessionStorage();
    }
} catch (e:Error) {
    // SecurityError or other
    trace("SharedObject unavailable: " + e.message);
    useSessionStorage();
}
```

**Impact on Evony:**
- Auto-login may not work
- Settings not persisted between sessions
- Last server selection lost

**CVE Relevance:**
- SharedObject itself has had vulnerabilities (CVE-2010-3637)
- Improper handling can leak path information
- Some CVEs allow unauthorized SharedObject access

**Security Best Practice:**
- Don't store sensitive data in SharedObject
- Validate data read from SharedObject
- Handle failures gracefully

**ErrorCode → GUI Dialog Mapping:**

**ErrorCode.as (Constants):**
```actionscript
public class ErrorCode {
    public static const SUCCESS:int = 0;
    public static const INVALID_PARAM:int = -1;
    public static const NOT_ENOUGH_RESOURCE:int = -10;
    public static const CASTLE_UNDER_PROTECTION:int = -52;
    // ... 200+ error codes
}
```

**Language File (Localization):**
```xml
<!-- en_US.xml -->
<error code="-10" message="Not enough resources"/>
<error code="-52" message="Target is under protection"/>
```

**Dialog Display Logic:**
```actionscript
// DialogManager.as
function showError(errorCode:int):void {
    var message:String = LanguageManager.getErrorMessage(errorCode);
    var dialog:AlertDialog = new AlertDialog();
    dialog.title = "Error";
    dialog.message = message;
    dialog.addButton("OK", closeDialog);
    PopupManager.addPopup(dialog);
}
```

**Flow:**
```
Server Response (code: -52)
    ↓
CommandHandler checks code < 0
    ↓
DialogManager.showError(-52)
    ↓
LanguageManager.getErrorMessage(-52)
    → "Target is under protection"
    ↓
AlertDialog rendered to user
```

**Cross-Domain Connection:**
- Protocol defines numeric error codes
- Enums provide named constants
- Localization maps to user-friendly text
- GUI renders the final message

**Army Movement → Animation Flow:**

**1. Protocol Event Received:**
```actionscript
// ArmyManager.as
function onMarchUpdate(event:DataEvent):void {
    var marchData:Object = event.data;
    // marchData.troopType = 7 (T_CATAPHRACT)
    // marchData.fromX, fromY, toX, toY
    // marchData.startTime, arrivalTime

    updateMarchVisual(marchData);
}
```

**2. Animation Lookup:**
```actionscript
// MapView.as
function updateMarchVisual(march:Object):void {
    var troopType:int = march.troopType;

    // Get animation ID from TFConstants → EvonyAnimation mapping
    var animId:int = getWalkAnimation(troopType);
    // TFConstants.T_CATAPHRACT (7) → EvonyAnimation.ANIM_CATAPHRACT_WALK (702)

    // Create or update march sprite
    var sprite:MarchSprite = marchSprites[march.marchId];
    sprite.playAnimation(animId);
    sprite.moveTo(march.toX, march.toY, march.arrivalTime - march.startTime);
}
```

**3. Animation Playback:**
```actionscript
// MarchSprite.as
function playAnimation(animId:int):void {
    var frames:Array = EvonyAnimation.getFrames(animId);
    // frames = [frame1.png, frame2.png, ...]

    animTimer = new Timer(100);  // 10 FPS
    animTimer.addEventListener(TimerEvent.TIMER, nextFrame);
    animTimer.start();
}
```

**Cross-Domain Flow:**
```
Server: army.marchUpdate
    ↓
Protocol: AMF deserialize → marchData object
    ↓
ArmyManager: Process march, dispatch event
    ↓
MapView: Look up animation for troop type
    ↓
EvonyAnimation: Return frame data
    ↓
MarchSprite: Animate on screen
```

**Constants Used:**
- TFConstants.T_CATAPHRACT = 7 (troop type)
- EvonyAnimation.ANIM_CATAPHRACT_WALK = 702 (visual)
- Animation frame rate, sprite assets
